ollows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})}{(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{2 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 4 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(- x^{2} + 2 x - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) e^{x} + 2}{\\left(e^{x} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488413 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488425 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488413 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488413 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x)=\\frac{x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$ wherever the denominator is nonzero." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26d2dda4-3244-5741-b97a-7622e9d53637" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488413 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 x + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + \\sin{\\left(