}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 x + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})}{(e^{x} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\left(- x^{2} + 2 x - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right) e^{x} + 2}{\\left(e^{x} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488448 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096621.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186488448 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "8e263c5f-b146-54ed-8643-53c90e74e85f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489467 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489467 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489467 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=24 x - 60 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ at the point $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "308d927b-9585-594c-b5e7-da139c2cdf56" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489467 #edb/ref 1074 "The slope is the derivative evaluated at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}.$\n\nWe know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin x)=\\cos x,$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x.$ Applying these formulas and the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(24 x - 60 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &= (60 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(24) \\\\ &= 60 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\ny^{\\prime}(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=24+60\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=24+60\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=54.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $54.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489494 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489470 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=22 x - 55 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ at the point $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44191e59-3ef1-56f2-b3ae-15156e95a80d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489470 #edb/ref 1074 "The slope is the derivative evaluated at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}.$\n\nWe know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin x)=\\cos x,$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x.$ Applying these formulas and the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(22 x - 55 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &= (55 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(22) \\\\ &= 55 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\ny^{\\prime}(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=22+55\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=22+55\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{99}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $\\frac{99}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489478 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489482 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489478 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489478 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of $y=- 16 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{8}{x^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489478 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7af3519e-f7d3-5ca4-a6bd-1048972ce066" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489478 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sin x)=\\cos x,$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\cos x)=-\\sin x.$ Applying these formulas and the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(- 16 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{8}{x^{2}}) \\\\ &= (16 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})+(- \\frac{16}{x^{3}}) \\\\ &= 16 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\frac{16}{x^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489489 #