+(6) \\\\ &= 15 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\ny^{\\prime}(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=6+15\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=6+15\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{27}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $\\frac{27}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489497 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186059675.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489497 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "2db58723-b530-57aa-afb2-4f64d6a53f46" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186492115 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096620.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186492115 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "17203972-63f6-5685-bfbe-c7073bcb6197" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493312 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x)=10 x^{2} + 5 x$ at the point $(1,15)$ intersects the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e3f1a4a-bfde-54af-80e2-4cc4e890e6fc" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493316 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 x^{2} + 5 x)=20 x + 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=25=25,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(25)}=- \\frac{1}{25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(15)&=- \\frac{1}{25}(x-(1))\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x-(- \\frac{1}{25})+(15)\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}&=0\\\\x&=376.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(376,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592