 1072 #uuid "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30)=36 x - 36.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(0)=-36=-36,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-36)}=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{36}(x-(0))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{36}x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x+30&=0\\\\\\frac{1}{36}x&=-30\\\\x&=-1080.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(-1080,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092385.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "6f93f05c-93ce-5432-b4e0-7ec958ee8e90" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092240.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "733357e0-41a3-5401-bdd5-4100649b68a2" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
